course: dictionary
lesson: 8147
title: A republic
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A republic is a country where the people choose their leaders. The clues are in the words around the word: «elected president» tells you that people vote for the head of the country.
explain: «The British monarch is also head of state of 14 other Commonwealth countries.» A monarch is a king or queen. Check your idea by swapping it in: a country with a king or queen is a monarchy, not a republic.
explain: Look at the names too: «the French Republic» and «the Republic of Ireland». When a word sits inside a country's full name, it tells you how that country is run.
fact: A republic is a country where the people choose their leaders.
fact: The head of state in a republic is usually an elected president, not a king or queen.
fact: A monarchy is a country with a king or queen as head of state.
fact: The USA, France, Ireland and Ukraine are republics.
fact: «Barbados became a republic in 2021», so it no longer has the British monarch as its head of state.
fact: «Republic» is part of many country names, such as the Republic of Ireland.
exercise: «A republic is a country where the people choose their leaders.» What is a republic? | A very large island | A country ruled by a king or queen | *A country where the people choose their leaders | A type of school
exercise: «The British monarch is also head of state of 14 other Commonwealth countries.» What is a monarch? | An elected president | A national flag | *A king or queen | A kind of parliament
exercise: Which of these countries is a republic? | *Ireland | The UK | Canada | Australia
test: «In 1999 Australians voted in a referendum on becoming a republic.» What would becoming a republic mean for Australia? | Winning a sports competition | Moving the capital city to another place | *Having a president instead of a king or queen | Having a new king or queen
test: Which of these was a republic before it had emperors? | Australia | *Ancient Rome | Canada | The UK
exam: «the Republic of Ireland» tells you about the country's government. What does the word Republic in its name tell you? | That the country has a king or queen | That the country is an island | That the country is very old | *That the people choose the country's leaders, with no king or queen as head of state
